WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.670
Let's not build another dashboard nobody will use.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:11.830
Because building with AI is exciting and promising, and also misleading: your first draft looks finished long before it's useful.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.130
Now, at Monday, you have plenty of great options, so starting is the easy part.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:25.630
But whichever you pick, working intentionally and gradually gets significantly better results than the hoping-for-the-best method.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.330
Which costs time and money, and hurts quality.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.010
That's because a big bang, all at once, often builds a monster: very impressive,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.890
and very hard to use.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.930
So in this adventure, you plan first, try a few quick drafts, and build gradually, testing on real work.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.150
Then you share it so people can trust it: they see who owns it and where the numbers come from.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.670
And this time, people open it

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.270
twice.
